\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 I walked slowly round him, taking him in. He was an old man. His skin was dry and papery, and the veins were thick and clotted in his hands. His eyes were large, dark and liquid, with magnificently hooded eyelids and arched eyebrows. His mouth was long and mobile, red and oddly wet. He wore a suit in a prince of wales check. He must have been thin for a long time because, although it was an old suit, it fitted him perfectly\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0  which is to say that it was wrinkele dand saggy because the fabric was old and worn, not because the cut was wrong.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He said with a rueful screwing up of his mouth.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Tensions had begun to appear within the group. Arne-Sayles had become highly sensitive to any remark or question that showed the speaker was insufficiently committed to his \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91great experiment\u8217\'92. Anyone who dared to question him was subjected to a savage raking-over of all their failings, personal and academic. Consequently,  most of the group maintained a diplomatic silence, but stanley ovenden, who had a sort of tone-deafness when it came to other people\u8217\'92s personalities, continued to express doubts about what they were doing. When Tali Hughes defended Ovenden to Aren-Sayles, she also came in for a generous share of his spleen. The atmospher bbecame increasingly tense and, as a result, Ovenden adn Hughes began spending more and more time away from the others.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Despite all this I believe that I was preciptate to dismiss these two entries as gibberish.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 It was sruprising to me that someone like 16, someone so wedded to Destruction and Madness, should wear a perfume so lovely, so redolent of Sunshine and Happiness.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91Put it back!\u8217\'92 I screamed at him.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He began to laugh.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 And he laughed, and laughed, and laughed.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Instantly, and to my huge embarrassment, I started crying. Great creaking sobs rose up in my chest and tears sprouted from my eyes. I did not think that it was me who was crying; it was matthew Rose Sorensen crying through my eyes. It lasted for a long tim until it tailed off into brayhing, hiccuping gulps for air.}}